rification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find every subset of $S,$ we list out every combination of elements within $S.$\n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/assets/022399e6a7a5e1f79b58e856aa8e9e5e9f3561e8e4bcb5b80a95237d30d06002.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,{r},{t},{r,t}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0667bfe035df587e2031bc104cc8b2f39e4702dc3fe27d88200b2f818d587e1" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{r,t}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{r},{t}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{r},{t},{r,t}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅,{r,t}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅,{r},{t},{r,t}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in Z∣x\\le 5}$ and $B={x\\in Z∣-7\\le x<3}?$\n\n- $A⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $B⊈A$\n- $A⊇B$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the integer numbers that satisfy the inequality $x\\le 5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA={…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality $-7\\le x<3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB={-7,-6,-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false.  For example, $5\\in A$ but $5\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true, while $B⊈A$ is false. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $A⊇B$ is equivalent to $B⊆A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0667bfe035df587e2031bc104cc8b2f39e4702dc3fe27d88200b2f818d587e1" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and IV only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III and IV only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and IV only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c423d5f5eb0233a5f008b1bbab00c39c8a481cf9eb95912a1cfa9d6af2fb0c" "basis" 2485 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-37266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets is a subset of $A={3,6,9,12,15,18,21,…}?$\n\n- $B={3n:n\\in N,1\\le n\\le 4}$\n- $C={6n:n\\in N,1\\le n\\le 3}$\n- $D={2n:n\\in N,1\\le n\\le 4}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the sets $B,C$ and $D.$\n\n- We find the elements of the set $B$ substituting the values $n\\in {1,2,3,4}$ into the formula $3n,$ and we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=1 & \\,⇒\\,3(1)=3 \\\\ n=2 & \\,⇒\\,3(2)=6 \\\\ n=3 & \\,⇒\\,3(3)=9 \\\\ n=4 & \\,⇒\\,3(4)=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have, $B={3,6,9,12}.$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $C$ can be found substituting the values $n\\in {1,2,3}$ into the formula $6n,$ and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=1 & \\,⇒\\,6(1)=6 \\\\ n=2 & \\,⇒\\,6(2)=12 \\\\ n=3 & \\,⇒\\,6(3)=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $C={6,12,18}.$\n\n- Finally, the elements of the set $D$ can be found substituting the values $n\\in {1,2,3,4}$ into the formula $2n,$ and we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=1 & \\,⇒\\,2(1)=2 \\\\ n=2 & \\,⇒\\,2(2)=4 \\\\ n=3 & \\,⇒\\,2(3)=6 \\\\ n=4 & \\,⇒\\,2(4)=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have, $D={2,4,6,8}.$\n\nNow, a set is a subset of $A$ if all of its elements are also elements of $A.$ With that in mind, let's inspect each option.\n\n- $B={3,6,9,12}$ is a subset of $A.\\,✓$\n\n- $C={6,12,18}$ is a subset of $A.\\,✓$\n\n- $D={2,4,6,8}$ is *not* a subset of $A$ because it contains the element $2\\notin A.\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "17b1b6a1bda16aa16216243c0938dd635ee848fa836b32d73e92f5ffaa4f5889"} {"question" "q-37266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets is a subset of $A={4n+1∣n\\in {0,1,2,3}}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the set $A.$ Substituting the values $n\\in {0,1,2,3}$ into the formula $4n+1,$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=0 & \\,⇒\\,4(0)+1=1 \\\\ n=1 & \\,⇒\\,4(1)+1=5 \\\\ n=2 & \\,⇒\\,4(2)+1=9 \\\\ n=3 & \\,⇒\\,4(3)+1=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA={1,5,9,13}.\n$$\n\nNow, a subset of $A$ is a set whose elements are also elements of the set $A.$\n\nIn our case, $B={1,5,13}$ is a subset of $A.$\n\nIn the rest of the options, the set $B$ has elements that are not in $A,$ meaning that it is not a subset of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "17b1b6a1bda16aa16216243c0938dd635ee848fa836b32d73e92f5ffaa4f5889"} {"question" "q-37264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={0,1,2,3}"] ["math" "B={0,1,5,9,13}"] ["math" "B={1,2,9,12}"] ["math" "B={1,5,13}"] ["math" "B={1,5,9,13,17}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={1,5,13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets is a subset of $A={2n∣n\\in N}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the set $A.$ The elements of the set \n$A$ are all the natural even numbers.\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA={2,4,6,8,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, a subset of $A$ is a set whose elements are also elements of the set $A.$\n\nIn our case, $B={2,6,12,14,32}$ is a subset of $A.$\n\nIn the rest of the options, the set $B$ has elements that are not in $A,$ meaning that it is not a subset of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "17b1b6a1bda16aa16216243c0938dd635ee848fa836b32d73e92f5ffaa4f5889"} {"question" "q-37265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={-1,0,1,2,4,6}"] ["math" "B={0,1,2,4,6,8}"] ["math" "B={1,3,5,7,9}"] ["math" "B={2,4,6,7}"] ["math" "B={2,6,12,14,32}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-37265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={2,6,12,14,32}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-1188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which set is a subset of $B={a,b,c,f}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-1188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A set is a subset of $B$ if all its elements are elements of $B.$\n\nOf the given sets, only ${c,f}$ has all of its elements in $B.$\n\nTherefore, ${c,f}$ is a subset of $B.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-1188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "17b1b6a1bda16aa16216243c0938dd635ee848fa836b32d73e92f5ffaa4f5889"} {"question" "q-1188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-1188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{a,b,c,e}"] ["math" "{a,b,e}"] ["math" "{a,c,d,e,f}"] ["math" "{a,c,d}"] ["math" "{c,f}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-1188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{c,f}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-1189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets is a subset of $A={1,2,3,4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-1189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A set is a subset of $A$ if all its elements are elements of $A.$\n\nNotice that the empty set ${}$ is a subset of any set.\n\nTherefore, ${}$ is a subset of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/state.json" "file_sha256" "6dda760ab79edc564fb0dab909b0f1b7ad2f41550167811b2c3edb30e4482af5"} {"question" "q-1189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/